WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.140
A cell should divide only when it is told to.

2
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:12.100
So every signaling pathway has an on step and an off step, The signal flips a switch

3
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.680
on, and the off step flips it back.

4
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:16.700
Now suppose the switch sticks.

5
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.920
The cell divides on its own.

6
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:23.880
There are two ways to make that happen: jam an on step or remove an off step.

7
00:00:24.583 --> 00:00:26.103
First, jam the on step.

8
00:00:26.783 --> 00:00:28.923
Ras is on while it holds GTP.

9
00:00:29.723 --> 00:00:35.343
Normally a helper called a GAP makes Ras break down that GTP, and the switch turns

10
00:00:35.343 --> 00:00:40.463
off. One changed amino acid, as in Ras G12V, slows this.

11
00:00:41.143 --> 00:00:45.003
Ras breaks down its GTP slowly, even with a GAP.

12
00:00:45.663 --> 00:00:48.443
A gene that can turn a cell cancerous is an oncogene.

13
00:00:49.217 --> 00:00:51.357
Second, remove the off -step.

14
00:00:52.197 --> 00:00:54.297
Neurofibramin is a GAP for Ras.

15
00:00:54.657 --> 00:00:55.757
It is the off -step.

16
00:00:56.517 --> 00:00:59.997
Lose neurofibromin, and Ras GTP is not cleared.

17
00:01:00.577 --> 00:01:02.157
No on -step is jammed here.

18
00:01:02.537 --> 00:01:03.797
An off -step is missing.

19
00:01:04.357 --> 00:01:08.537
A gene whose loss lets cells grow when they should not is a tumour suppressor.

20
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.200
Now count the copies.

21
00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:14.840
You carry two copies of nearly every gene, one from each parent.

22
00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.280
Suppose one copy of the Ras gene is changed.

23
00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:21.260
The altered protein signals without being told to.

24
00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.680
The normal protein from the other copy cannot stop it.

25
00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:25.880
So the cell divides.

26
00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:29.620
This is a gain of function, and it is dominant.

27
00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:32.740
It shows even when the other copy is normal.

28
00:01:33.583 --> 00:01:35.023
An off switch is different.

29
00:01:35.783 --> 00:01:38.803
One good copy usually makes enough protein to do the job.

30
00:01:39.403 --> 00:01:42.943
Lose one copy of the gene, and the off step still works.

31
00:01:43.623 --> 00:01:46.403
Both copies must go before the off step fails.

32
00:01:47.523 --> 00:01:50.363
Alfred Knudson proposed two hits for retinoblastoma.

33
00:01:51.023 --> 00:01:53.983
The two hits turned out to be the two copies of one gene.

34
00:01:54.817 --> 00:01:58.137
So a stuck switch follows two rules, whichever way it sticks.

35
00:01:58.597 --> 00:02:01.337
A jammed on step acts when one copy is altered.

36
00:02:01.917 --> 00:02:04.737
A lost off step usually needs both copies gone.

37
00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:08.197
Gain acts alone. Loss needs both.
